      "card_ids": ["C05", "C12", "C16", "C18", "C39"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Tegafur, a related heteroaromatic oral drug, has almost complete human bioavailability and 43.8% oral bioavailability in dogs.",
      "card_ids": ["C01", "C20", "C26", "C36"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 tedizolid data provide a direct oral-versus-IV exposure ratio: oral AUC 26.1 vs IV 30.5 µg·h/mL (~86%) and Cmax 2.25 vs 3.02 µg/mL (~75%), supporting high F in a structurally related fluorophenyl heteroaromatic drug.",
      "card_ids": ["C52", "C45"]
    }
  ],
