      "card_ids": ["C43", "C46", "C47"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement or matched oral-versus-IV AUC exists for the query molecule.",
    "L3 records are for reference molecules (voriconazole, doravirine, tedizolid), not the query; transfer is structural/contextual.",
    "No query-specific Cmax or AUC data are available.",
    "Solubility/dissolution and first-pass metabolism for the query are not experimentally measured; low Fsp3 and multiple aromatic rings could affect formulation-dependent absorption.",
    "Cmax-only records for voriconazole and doravirine do not by themselves establish F >=20%."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F >= 20%) maintained and strengthened: the closest structural context (compound 19) reports predicted human F=80% and measured rat/dog F=63-71%; voriconazole, aprepitant, and tegafur contexts all exceed 20%; L3 adds a tedizolid oral/IV AUC ratio of ~86% and consistent oral Cmax exposure records, with no affirmative evidence for F <20%."
}

